   $\{y:\psi(y^{n},y)\le c\}$ are compact in $Y$;
\item[(B)] (\emph{Borelness})  
   $\mathscr{F}$ is a \emph{Borel} (equivalently Suslin) subset of
   $C(Y^{n+1},\mathbb{R})$ endowed with the compact-open topology.
\end{description}
Then, the (Full) Conformal
Prediction correspondence \( \kappa \) on $X_+$ is compact-valued and weakly measurable. If we consider the correspondence on the whole space $X$, then we also need to require that $Y$ is compact.
\end{theorem}


