We now ask ourselves whether we can find monads on the categories $\mathbf{UHCont}$ and \(\mathbf{WMeas}_\text{uc}\). The general answer is no, but we can find interesting subcategories for which a monad can be found.

\begin{definition}[Structure \(\mathbf{UHCont}^{\mathrm{cH}}_\text{c}\)]\label{def-chcorr}
Define the structure \(\mathbf{UHCont}^{\mathrm{cH}}_\text{c}\) as follows,
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Objects:} {\em Compact Hausdorff} spaces \(X\).
  \item \textbf{Morphisms:} {\em Compact-valued}, upper hemicontinuous \(\Phi : X \rightrightarrows Y\).
\end{itemize}
\end{definition}

It is immediate to see that structure \(\mathbf{UHCont}^{\mathrm{cH}}_\text{c}\) is a subcategory of \(\mathbf{UHCont}\). It admits a monad.
