Next, using the verified eigenpairs shown in \cref{fig:sealevelevals} and the arguments of \cref{sec:errorcontrolpfmd}, we compute predictions of future Northern Hemisphere sea level heights and compare them to the simulated values. As before, we compare the relative errors of our method to those of DMD and kEDMD, and the results are shown in \cref{fig:sealevelerror}. Our RKHS approach achieved dramatically better  forecasts than standard DMD or kEDMD. Moreover, our model uses only 5 modes versus 299 for kEDMD – a 98\% reduction in model complexity.


