\subsection{Runtime Resource Cost}
\label{Subsection: Runtime Resource Cost}
To obtain a better understanding of OpenSN, we investigate the runtime resource cost (i.e., CPU and memory).
In this experiment, we use a four-VM cluster with a total of 64 vCPU and 128GB memory for both OpenSN and StarryNet.
Fig.~\ref{fig: resource-cost} compares the real-time resource usage of OpenSN and StarryNet.
The two sub-figures correspond to emulating OneWeb constellation and Starlink Shell-I constellation.
