The first relation suggests that the coordinate $y_5$ is a linear function in the variables $(z_{92},y_{92})$ intersecting the exceptional curve $\mathcal{F}_9$, i.e.\ we set 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:syst_92_intermediate}
    y_5 \colon a_{10}\,z_{92} + a_{01}\,y_{92}+a_{00} \,,
\end{equation}
with $a_{ij}=a_{ij}(x)$, and we require that this line goes through the point $(U_0,V_0)=(0,0)$ in~\eqref{eq:syst_92_cascades}. We rewrite~\eqref{eq:syst_92_intermediate} in the chart $(U_0,V_0)$, obtaining 
\begin{equation}
    a_{10}\,U_0 + a_{01}+a_{00}\,V_0 = 0\,,
\end{equation}
and imposing that the point $(U_0,V_0)=(0,0)$ is part of the line we find the condition $a_{01}=0$. The second expression in~\eqref{eq:ax_5_92} is a conic in the variables $(z_{92},y_{92})$, i.e.\
\begin{equation}\label{eq:z_5_conic_92}
