\subsubsection{Results:} \cref{DMD_kreiss_fig} (left) shows the pseudospectrum computed by ResDMD, as well as the DMD eigenvalues (red dots). On the circle, a lattice of eigenvalues corresponds to harmonics on the limit cycle generated by an eigenfunction $g_0$ with eigenvalue $\lambda_0$ (green dot). The lattice structure arises since the Koopman operator is multiplicative: $K[g_1g_2]=[Kg_1][Kg_2]$. These harmonics are shown in \cref{DMD_eigenfunction_fig}, where we plot the eigenfunctions corresponding to $\lambda_0$, $\lambda_0^2$, and $\lambda_0^3$ across the entire state space $\mathbb{R}^{20}$. Here, the interpretation is that each two-dimensional block of $\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{20}$ corresponds to marching the eigenfunction backward in time, capturing dynamics off the limit cycle.

\cref{DMD_kreiss_fig} (left) also shows large regions of pseudospectra corresponding to transient (off-limit cycle) behavior. \cref{DMD_kreiss_fig} (right) shows the Kreiss constant of the Koopman operator as $h$ varies.

