\begin{abstract}
This study considers 
the Merton model with temporal correlation.
We show  the  Merton model becomes Poisson process with
the log-normal distributed intensity function
in the  limit.
We discuss the relation between this model and Hawkes process.
In this model we confirm the super-normal transition when the  temporal correlation is power case.
The phase  transition is  same as  seen before the limit.
We apply this model to the default portfolios and  find that  the power decay model provides better generalization performance for the long term data.



