\!
\cdot 
b_{s-1}^{-1} 
\cdot 
g^{-1}\}
$ and  
$\Y=\{l_{s-1,\; 0},\ldots,l_{s-1,\; s-1}\}$
we see that any element $w$ from $\langle \X
, \Y \rangle \le \Lambda_s$ is a product of elements of $g_{f^+}^{\vphantom{1}} \!
\cdot 
b_{s-1}^{-1} 
