\end{equation} 
Notice that we do \textit{not} include the relations telling that $a,b,c$ commute with $z, r,\, s, l$ (to reflect the direct product $F \times \mathcal L$) because 
$K_{\!\mathcal X}$ already includes $F$, and so the third line of \eqref{EQ relations KQ} already is enough. 
If $K_{\!\mathcal X}$ has $m$ generators (which we may assume include $a,b,c$) and $n$ defining relations, and if 
