\subsection{Trade-off Analysis}
To further investigate the trade-off between multi-user communication and target sensing performance, we vary the achievable rate threshold $\gamma$ in the optimization problem (\ref{initial}) and plot the resulting trade-off curves. Fig.~\ref{Sim:trade_off} illustrates the relationship between the achievable communication rate and the target position RMSE and velocity RMSE. As the required achievable rate increases, both the position RMSE and the velocity RMSE increase, indicating a degradation in sensing accuracy. This confirms the fundamental trade-off between communication and sensing performance in the considered cell-free ISAC system.



