    For a representation $\phi$ in $\HP(\Sigma_{0,3})$ with  $e(\phi)=n$, 
     let $\widetilde{\phi(c_i)},$  $i \in\{ 1,2,3\},$  be the unique lift of $\phi(c_i)$ in $\overline{\Hyp_0}$. Since $\ev(\phi)=\widetilde{\phi(c_1)}\widetilde{\phi(c_2)}= z^n\widetilde{\phi(c_3)}^{-1} \in \overline{\Hyp_n}$, 
     the image of $\phi$ under the map $\ev$ lies in $\overline{\Hyp_n}$.
