            %we have $g_1\neq\pm  \mathrm{I}$ and $g_2\neq\pm  \mathrm{I}$, 
            as otherwise $\ev(g_1,g_2) \in \overline{\Hyp_0}$. It follows that the pair $(g_1,g_2)$ lies in one of the following sets: $\Hyp\times \Hyp$, 
            $\Hyp\times \Par$, 
            $\Par\times \Hyp$, 
