            Since $\widetilde{g_{1,1}g_{2,1}} =\widetilde{g_1}\widetilde{g_2} \notin \overline{\Hyp_0}$, the paths $\{g_{1,t}\}\interval$ and $\{g_{2,t}\}\interval$ are not contained in a common one-parameter subgroup of $\psl$, as otherwise the path $\{\widetilde{g_{1,t}g_{2,t}}\}\interval$ is entirely contained in $\overline{\Hyp_0}$. As a consequence, for all $t\in (0,1]$, the lift of $g_{2,t}$ to $\SL$ is not a diagonal matrix. Hence either $ab\neq 0$ or $cd\neq 0$, which implies that $\widetilde{g_{1,t}g_{2,t}}\neq z^{\pm 1}$ for all $t\in [0,1]$. Moreover, for any $t$ such that $\widetilde{g_{1,t}g_{2,t}}\in \Par_{\pm 1}$, Lemma \ref{lem_offdiag} implies that the sign of $\widetilde{g_{1,t}g_{2,t}}
