     where $c_1, c_2, c_3$, and $c_4$ are the preferred peripheral elements.
     Let $P_1\cup P_2$ be a pants decomposition of $\Sigma_{0,4}$, where $P_1 \cong\Sigma_{0,3}$ with $\pi_1(P_1) = \langle c_1, c_2 \rangle$ and $P_2 \cong \Sigma_{0,3}$ with $\pi_1(P_2) = \langle c_3, c_4 \rangle$, separated by a decomposition curve $d = c_3c_4 = (c_1c_2)^{-1}$.
     \\

