         By Theorem \ref{thm_nonabel}, we can assume that $\phi|_{\pi_1(P_1)}$, $\phi|_{\pi_1(P_2)}$, $\psi|_{\pi_1(P_1)}$ and $\psi|_{\pi_1(P_2)}$ are non-abelian; and by Lemma \ref{lem_inthyppants}, we can assume that $\phi(d)$ and $\psi(d)$ are hyperbolic, and $\phi|_{\pi_1(P_1)}, \psi|_{\pi_1(P_1)}\in \HP(P_1)$. Under these assumptions, for each $n$ satisfying $-1\leqslant n\leqslant 2$,
        we will find a path in $\HPns(\pantstwo)$ connecting $\phi$ to $\psi$.
        \smallskip

