\section{General surfaces}
     In this section, we complete the proof of Theorem \ref{thm_main1} and Theorem \ref{thm_main4} for general punctured surfaces. Corresponding to the Cases (2) and (3) in Theorem \ref{thm_main2}, for $\Sigma = \Sigma_{g,p}$, $n\in \mathbb{Z}$ and $s\in \{-1,0,+1\}^p$, we will call the triple $(\Sigma, n,s)$ \emph{exceptional} if $g = 0$, $p_0(s) = 0$, and the pair $(n,s)$ satisfies one of the following conditions:
    \begin{enumerate}[(1)]
