            As $\lambda$ varies from $0$ to $4,$ the trace $\tr(A_\theta)=2-\lambda$ decreses from $2$ to $-2$.
            Moreover, whenever $\tr(A_\theta)\in (-2,2)$, the corresponding $\widetilde{g_1}\widetilde{g_2}$ is elliptic as it projects to $A_\theta$ in $\SL$, hence lies in $\Ell_s$ as shown in the previous paragraph. 
