    For (2), by Lemma \ref{lem_plp} and Lemma \ref{lem_evPsubm}, it suffices to show that for all $\widetilde{C}\in \Ell_s$, the fiber $\ev^{-1}(\widetilde{C})$ is connected in $\PP^s(\Sigma_{0,3})$. 
    Let $\widetilde{C}\in \Ell_s$, and let $\phi_1, \phi_2\in \PP^s(\Sigma_{0,3})$ such that $\ev(\phi_1) = \ev(\phi_2) = \widetilde{C}$. 
    We will construct a path  
     $\{\phi'_t\}_{t\in [1,2]}$ 
