 Abstract}\end{center} \vspace{0.4cm}
$~~~$The constrained filed system, the scalar field coupled to two flavours of fermions through
Yukawa couplings, is treated by using the
Hamilton-Jacobi approach. The equations of motion are obtained as
total differential equations in many variables. The equations of
motion are in exact agreement with those equations obtained using
Dirac's method. Due to the Hamilton-Jacobi quantization, the path integral 
of the scalar field coupled to two fermions is obtained directly
as an integration over the canonical phase space without using any gauge fixing condition.
